Updating Edge Weight and Detecting a Disconnected Graph
Start.
Create a weighted graph representing airport facilities and their ground connections.
Input the number of vertices and the edge weights.
Display the graph and ask the user to select an edge for updating.
Update the selected edge with the new weight.
Initialize all vertices as unvisited and select a starting vertex.
Apply Prim’s algorithm to find the minimum-weight edge connecting a visited vertex to an unvisited vertex.
Select the minimum-weight edge, mark the new vertex as visited, and update the running total cost.
Repeat Steps 7 and 8 until all vertices are visited or no connecting edge is available.
If all vertices are visited, display every selected edge with its weight and the running total cost.
If some vertices remain unvisited, display a message that the graph is disconnected and a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) cannot be formed.
Stop.
